{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>All the congregation.</b> He mentioned 'all the congregation' because Edom came out to meet them to do battle with them, and in order to make known that not one of them was missing when they came from the land of Edom to Mount Hor." "<b>And they said</b> in the Midrash: Mount Hor — a mountain upon a mountain, like a small apple on a large apple. And Aaron was buried in that place whose name is Hor, as it says (Numbers 33:39), ״וימת אהרן שם בראש ההר״. And even though the cloud went before them and leveled the mountains, three mountains remained: Mount Sinai for the Torah, Mount Hor for the burial of Aaron, and Mount Nebo for the burial of Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:23.322392254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}